# One shared cron example. Point DIR at the sol1 port you actually run.
# flock: a poll that runs longer than the interval must not start another.
# logger: a cron job with nowhere to write is a cron job whose failures
# reach you from a confused colleague.
#
# Install:
#   crontab -e
# then paste, after editing DIR and the interval.
#
# Live run of this file against every port: not tried. The wiring is the
# example. See the coverage table in the lab README.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
DIR=/opt/agents/solutions/sol1_enhancer
LOG=/var/log/enhancer-poll.log

*/10 * * * * flock -n /tmp/enhancer-poll.lock -c "cd $DIR && task run" >> $LOG 2>&1
